From 2c42824b639ea826e3d97cc2643538f09cc0e02d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yolobox <yolobox@phaer.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:51:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] launchers: follow exports propagate for env

When collecting env vars for launch records, runtime-env now follows the
exports.propagate chain transitively using dep-closure. Before this
change, only direct dependencies contributed env vars; propagated
packages were ignored.

The change makes launcher behavior match build-time behavior, where
prepare.nu already uses dep-closure for the same purpose.

Design decisions:
- PATH prepend stays direct-deps-only (propagated packages are libraries)
- Direct deps win on env conflict (closure is reversed before merge)
- All values stay `default` semantics (user env wins)

Performance: one small JSON read per propagated package. Typical
closures have 1-5 extra packages. No measurable finish-time impact.

Test: three packages (propagate-c exports env, propagate-b propagates
it, propagate-a links b only) verify the full chain reaches the
launch record.

Signed-off-by: yolobox <yolobox@phaer.org>
